Context
-------
Asked for a guile-skills repo suggesting how to start a project that exposes
guile3 --debug --listen=PORT, plus a debugging proxy on PORT+1 logging to
~/.guile-skill/projects/{pwd | tr / -}, in the shape of ~/.claude/projects.
Follow-on asks in the same session: log rotation, document the experiments and
deviations, Emacs+Geiser through the proxy, and the standard collaborators.

Inputs
------
- jwalsh/37d0ef2d6837e9234a878991d3c01c78 section 3.1 (Surfaces): a surface is
  what a worker can read or drive from its own tools; presence is not
  reachability; a GUI-first debugger is not a surface. Cloned to
  ~/ghq/gist.github.com/jwalsh/.
- aygp-dr/58f58a9ca6a44cc0570106999a96a9b1: the Clojure census handoff. Supplied
  the 007 thesis, the anti-pattern rankings (22/~19/14/8/8/6/3 of 75 skills), the
  no-linter gap, and the Guix-Home delivery finding. Also two measurements from
  hydra that this design rests on: --listen binds loopback only, and the wire
  protocol is the plain REPL rather than a framed one, so no bencode equivalent
  is needed.

Deviations
----------
- Proxy written in Guile rather than socat or shell. A socat tee would be
  shorter, but the log needs rendering (direction markers, ms timestamps,
  non-UTF-8 chunks reported instead of corrupting the file), and this is a Guile
  tooling repo.
- No style guide, deliberately. Experiment 007 found Clojure skills police
  tooling and process, not idioms -- Java-style loops drew zero warnings across
  75 skills. Writing one would have been the obvious wrong move.
- Port derivation (37000 + cksum(slug) mod 900) began as an admitted convention.
  On learning of portclaim mid-session it became a real reservation: 37496 and
  37497 are claimed as nexus-guile-skills-repl and -repl-proxy. The whole
  37000-37999 range was unclaimed, which is why the base sits there.
- Serial accept loop, not threaded. Geiser plus an agent simultaneously needs two
  proxies or a rewrite. Named in EXPERIMENTS.org "Still open" rather than
  pre-solved.

Considerations
--------------
- Four of six failures were silent, which is the argument for the whole
  repository. The worst was a stale proxy from an earlier test: it held the port,
  the replacement's bind failed uncaught and died quietly, and the old process
  kept answering tests while writing to a log nobody was reading. Three separate
  fixes (bind guard with errno, server refuses a taken port, --status/--stop).
- Every earlier test used nc -N, which half-closes after each send. Geiser holds
  one connection across many round-trips. Testing only the convenient client
  tested only half the connection lifecycle; E6 covers the other half now.
- Version disagreement with the other agent (3.0.10 here, 3.0.11 on hydra) was
  not taken at face value and not dismissed. Both are correct; nexus is FreeBSD
  15.1, hydra is 14.4. Recorded in README provenance as an instance of the very
  anti-pattern the table names.
- Claims are tagged measured-here / measured-on-hydra / inherited-from-Clojure /
  not-established. The unestablished three (,locals behaviour, GOOPS reload
  semantics, guile-lsp-server maturity) are flagged so they are checked before
  becoming instructions.

